course: dictionary
lesson: 11971
title: Catering: food for groups
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Catering means providing food and drink for an event or a group of people, usually as a job. «The catering company made 120 sandwiches for the wedding.» The clue is wedding: a company that feeds lots of guests is doing catering.
explain: Catering can also be a verb. To cater for people is to provide what a group needs or wants. «The café caters for vegans as well as meat-eaters.» The café does not just sell food; it thinks about what its customers want to eat.
explain: Self-catering is a word you may see in holiday adverts. «We booked a self-catering cottage, so we cooked all our own meals.» The word self tells you that you do the job yourself, so in a self-catering holiday you cook for yourself.
fact: Catering means providing food and drink for an event or a group of people.
fact: Catering is usually an uncountable noun, so we say «the catering» or «good catering», not «a catering» for a meal.
fact: «Cater for» means to provide what a group needs or wants.
fact: «Self-catering» means you cook for yourself, such as in a holiday cottage.
fact: School catering staff run the canteen and make lunches for the pupils.
exercise: «The catering company made 120 sandwiches for the party.» What is catering? | Sending invitations to guests | *Providing food and drink for a group of people, as a job | Driving the guests home | Cleaning up after a party
exercise: «Our holiday cottage was self-catering, so we bought food and cooked every night.» What does self-catering mean? | *You cook for yourself | You eat only sandwiches | You stay at a school | You get your meals served by a hotel
exercise: Ella plans a party: «There are 60 guests, and each guest eats 2 sandwiches.» How many sandwiches does the catering need? | 602 | 30 | *120 | 62
test: «The café caters for vegans and vegetarians.» What does cater for mean here? | *Provides what the customers need or want | Hides the menu from customers | Charges the most money for the food | Chops and cooks the vegetables
test: Which word means you cook your own meals on holiday? | Canteen | Catering | Holiday camp | *Self-catering
exam: «The school canteen is run by the catering team, who make lunch for every pupil.» What is the catering team's job? | *Making food and drink for the pupils | Selling tickets for the school play | Teaching maths to the pupils | Cleaning the classrooms
